# Server / Express API

## Language & Module System

Plain JavaScript with CommonJS (`require`/`module.exports`). Do NOT use TypeScript or ESM in the server workspace.

## Route Pattern

Every route file exports a named router (`{ fooRouter }`). Mount under `/api/` in `app.js`.

```js
const fooRouter = express.Router();
// ... handlers ...
module.exports = { fooRouter };
```

## Request Validation

Use `express-validator` (body/param/query) inline before handlers. Always call `validationResult(req)` at the top of the handler and return 400 early on failure.

## Error Handling

Pass errors to `next(err)`. The central `errorHandler` middleware formats them as `{ ok: false, error: { message, status } }`. Never send raw errors to the client.

## Auth Middleware

- `verifyToken` — extracts JWT from `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, sets `req.user { id, username, role }`.
- `requireRole(role)` / `requireAnyRole([...roles])` — guards by role (`admin`, `editor`).
- Public endpoints (e.g. `POST /api/bookings`, `GET /api/services`, `GET /api/content/:lang`) skip auth.

## Database Access

Import `{ query, withClient }` from `../config/db`. Use parameterized queries (`$1`, `$2`, ...) exclusively. Use `withClient` + `BEGIN`/`COMMIT`/`ROLLBACK` for transactions.

## ISR Revalidation

After content or services writes, call `triggerRevalidate('content')` or `triggerRevalidate('services')` (fire-and-forget) to refresh the Next.js static pages.
